pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* The one shape for which a contradiction inside a proofgoal scope legitimately discharges the
* enclosing proof-by-contradiction subproof, and which the fix for the fabricated-proofgoal
* defect therefore has to keep ACCEPTING.
*
* `red` with an empty witness is a proof by contradiction, and its goal `#1` is `C|<empty> = C`,
* so the premise the goal scope adds is `~C` -- the very constraint the subproof already carries.
* A contradiction derived there really is a contradiction from `~C`.
f 1
red 1 x1 >= 1 ; ; begin
    proofgoal #1
        u >= 1 ;
    end
end
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
